    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89646" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσκορής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>satiating, palling,
			tedious</i>, of a speech, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Inv.</u>
				3.10
			</span></i>; of a person, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Id.</u>
				2.11
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DMort.</u>
				26.2
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1055
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>sated</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.109
			</span></i> K.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span> with . . , <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				3.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσκόρως</span> (as if from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσκορος</span>) <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				4.3.3
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. χρῆσθαι κόσμῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hermog.
					<u>Id.</u>
					2.11
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγος π. κεκοσμημένος</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				1.12
			</span></i>.</div>
